 ### Fixed
+- **`ctx_edit` auto-escalation no longer strips the lines you were editing.**
+  After an `old_string` miss on a file read in a compressed mode, files over 300
+  lines were re-shown as head+tail with the middle `[... N lines omitted ...]`,
+  yet the cache was marked fully delivered — so a follow-up `ctx_read(mode="full")`
+  returned an `[unchanged]` stub and the stripped lines were unreachable, making
+  every retry fail. The escalation now shows a verbatim window centred on the
+  closest match to `old_string` and leaves the cache undelivered, so a full or
+  `lines:N-M` re-read returns real content.
 - **The Codex `lean-ctx -c` SessionStart hook is no longer a redundant nag (#625).**
   Codex's `PreToolUse` hook already rewrites every rewritable Bash command to
   `lean-ctx -c "<command>"` transparently (`permissionDecision: allow` +
